Package: spikeWatch
Type: Package
Title: Run Accuracy and Drift from Spike-in Truth
Version: 0.99.0
Authors@R: person("Amirhossein", "Daneshpajouh", role = c("aut", "cre"),
    email = "52765136+Daneshpajouh@users.noreply.github.com")
Description: Turns the known amounts of spike-in controls into accuracy
    figures for every run and tracks them across runs. One data model
    covers feature-level designs such as the ERCC RNA mixes and
    sample-level designs such as UPS1 dilution series in proteomics: the
    known amounts sit in an assay beside the measurements. Per run it
    reports the dose-response slope and fit, the detection limit and the
    overall response; between groups it reports fold-change accuracy.
    Across runs it charts any of these figures with Shewhart, EWMA or
    CUSUM charts against a baseline, to show drift across runs; the
    charts are exploratory: at the default limits, 15.7 to 35.2 percent of
    simulated drift-free series in the base family raised a false alarm
    within 20 runs, and 36.7 to 87.3 percent when runs were correlated,
    so their limits need checking on local runs.
